<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">It began at home.</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Patrick Peyton grew up on a farm in County Mayo, Ireland, one of nine children. Each evening, his father John led the family in the Rosary. His mother Mary and his grandparents shared the faith that shaped his childhood.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Prayer was something they did together. Years later, that experience would become the heart of his life’s work.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

</div><!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:image {"className":"fr-story-chapter-image"} --><figure class="wp-block-image fr-story-chapter-image"><img src="https://fatherpeyton.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2025/08/Peyton_Parents.webp" alt="Mary and John Peyton in an archival portrait."/><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Patrick’s parents, Mary and John Peyton.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->

</section><!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-story-chapter fr-story-beginnings","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section"} --><section class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-story-chapter fr-story-beginnings">
<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-story-chapter-copy","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-story-chapter-copy">
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">A priest with a family’s prayer in his heart.</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Patrick came to America with his brother Tom. In Scranton, Pennsylvania, work at the cathedral helped reawaken his desire to become a priest. Both brothers entered the Congregation of Holy Cross.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On June 15, 1941, they were ordained at Notre Dame. Father Patrick’s first assignment took him to Albany, New York. There, he began asking others to help bring the Rosary into family homes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-story-milestone"} --><p class="fr-story-milestone">1942 · The invitation begins to travel.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Students helped prepare letters to bishops. A mission that had begun around one family’s prayer was finding its way to other homes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

</div><!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:image {"className":"fr-story-chapter-image"} --><figure class="wp-block-image fr-story-chapter-image"><img src="https://www.familyrosary.org/hs-fs/hubfs/assets/Timeline/1942-min.png?width=960&amp;name=1942-min.png" alt="Father Peyton with students and a religious sister preparing the ministry’s work."/><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Albany, New York, 1942. Father Peyton planning a bishops’ mailing with students.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->

</section><!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-story-chapter fr-story-media","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section"} --><section class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-story-chapter fr-story-media">
<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-story-chapter-copy","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-story-chapter-copy">
<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">The message found a microphone.<br>Then a camera.</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On May 13, 1945, a national radio broadcast brought Father Peyton’s invitation to American families. Bing Crosby joined the program. Father Peyton asked listeners to pray the Rosary together for peace.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Family Theater Productions followed in 1947. Radio dramas, television and film gave him new ways to carry the same message. The Life of Christ films, completed in 1958, brought the mysteries of the Rosary to the screen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The medium changed. The invitation remained: pray together.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><a class="text-link" href="https://fatherpeyton.org/chapters/chapter-3/">Follow his work in radio and film</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->

</div><!-- /wp:group -->
